WEBVTT

00:16.976 --> 00:18.728
[Boyd] Previously on From...

00:18.811 --> 00:22.064
Everything's so... nice

00:22.148 --> 00:25.109
in that place I've seen.

00:25.609 --> 00:26.569
Victor...

00:26.652 --> 00:28.320
he wears a shirt and tie.

00:28.654 --> 00:31.657
And we have a grandson.

00:31.741 --> 00:34.076
He has your eyes.

00:34.160 --> 00:37.204
These things I'm seeing...

00:37.288 --> 00:39.123
could they be real?

00:39.206 --> 00:40.458
[heart monitor beeping]

00:40.541 --> 00:41.751
Do you want
to stay here, Henry?

00:41.834 --> 00:43.461
How?

00:43.544 --> 00:46.380
You have to
forcibly disconnect.

00:46.464 --> 00:48.799
You have to
eliminate the anchor.

00:50.509 --> 00:51.802
This morning, I saw this.

00:54.764 --> 00:57.767
Is it possible that I'm
turning into one of them?

00:57.850 --> 00:59.393
No.

00:59.477 --> 01:01.103
That's not
what's happening.

01:01.187 --> 01:02.605
Tell her that's
not what's happening.

01:02.688 --> 01:05.816
Her heart rate
is 19 beats per minute.

01:05.900 --> 01:07.276
That's impossible.

01:07.359 --> 01:09.236
Fatima shouldn't even
be alive right now.

01:10.821 --> 01:12.823
This is the chamber where
the bones are buried, right?

01:12.907 --> 01:14.492
What happens when they block

01:14.575 --> 01:16.660
our only exit out
of that chamber?

01:21.664 --> 01:23.167
We are standing

01:23.250 --> 01:26.253
right above the cavern
those bones are buried in.

01:26.337 --> 01:27.630
You wanna cut
down the tree?

01:27.713 --> 01:29.840
I wanna pull it
out by the roots.

01:29.924 --> 01:32.634
What's plan B, when the
tree doesn't come out

01:32.718 --> 01:35.179
and we have people
barricaded in a death trap

01:35.262 --> 01:37.306
with no place else to go?

01:37.389 --> 01:39.140
You're probably
gonna lose some people,

01:39.225 --> 01:40.559
but you could
save a whole lot more.

01:40.643 --> 01:43.354
So, suck it up, make a choice,
and live with it.

01:45.231 --> 01:48.609
[Thomas] Come to the RV
or I'll hurt Julie and Ethan.

01:50.360 --> 01:52.446
You're about to do something
you've never done before.

01:52.530 --> 01:53.489
[whimpering]

01:53.572 --> 01:55.157
You may have finally found

01:55.241 --> 01:58.619
the key to setting
those children free. Or...

01:58.702 --> 02:00.746
you're about to unleash

02:00.830 --> 02:05.417
a type of suffering you
can't even begin to imagine.

02:05.501 --> 02:06.836
[gasps]

02:06.919 --> 02:08.711
This was really nice.

02:10.548 --> 02:12.424
Oh, my God...

02:16.387 --> 02:18.180
He was
in my house, Boyd.

02:18.264 --> 02:19.723
That fucking thing
was in my house!

02:19.807 --> 02:21.225
-Wait. Are you sure?
-Yes!

02:21.308 --> 02:22.935
He had Ethan's drawings!

02:23.018 --> 02:24.353
That means he came inside!

02:24.436 --> 02:25.896
Even with a talisman
on the door,

02:25.980 --> 02:29.316
it was inside,
in the middle of the day.

02:31.610 --> 02:33.237
[softly]
Okay. All right.

02:35.948 --> 02:37.616
He killed Jim.

02:37.700 --> 02:39.535
What?
How do you know that?

02:39.618 --> 02:40.744
Because he told me!

02:40.828 --> 02:44.206
-Jesus...
-We're not safe here anymore.

02:45.583 --> 02:47.501
Look, hey.
I get it, Boyd.

02:47.585 --> 02:49.587
Okay? I know you want
to protect everybody.

02:49.670 --> 02:51.463
I know you want to
keep everyone safe,

02:51.547 --> 02:52.840
so do I.

02:54.966 --> 02:57.428
That's why I'm gonna be the one
going down into those tunnels.

02:57.511 --> 02:59.638
Boyd, listen, there is no

02:59.722 --> 03:01.265
perfect version
of a plan, all right?

03:01.348 --> 03:03.392
This is it; this is
the best chance we've got!

03:03.475 --> 03:05.227
You're right.

03:05.311 --> 03:07.897
-What?
-Walk me through it again.

03:07.980 --> 03:09.648
Wait.
What just happened?

03:09.732 --> 03:12.568
That guy in
the yellow suit, he's back.

03:12.651 --> 03:14.236
When the sun
comes up tomorrow,

03:14.320 --> 03:16.572
I wanna be ready to
put shovels in the ground.

03:16.655 --> 03:18.282
We're getting
those fucking bones.

03:22.036 --> 03:23.329
[sighs]

03:25.748 --> 03:27.374
[tense music playing]

03:35.841 --> 03:39.428
[groaning]

03:39.511 --> 03:41.388
[bones cracking]

03:41.472 --> 03:42.430
[groaning]

03:42.514 --> 03:46.644
[bones cracking]

03:46.727 --> 03:47.686
[groaning]

03:47.770 --> 03:49.021
[bones cracking]

03:49.103 --> 03:51.982
[screaming]

04:05.829 --> 04:07.623
What are you guys doing?

04:07.706 --> 04:09.667
Boyd told us to gather

04:09.750 --> 04:10.751
all the rope
and chain we could find.

04:10.834 --> 04:11.752
For what?

04:11.835 --> 04:13.629
You didn't hear?

04:13.712 --> 04:15.839
When people go into
the tunnels tomorrow,

04:15.923 --> 04:17.423
they're gonna
dig up those bones.

04:17.507 --> 04:18.425
Really?

04:18.509 --> 04:20.386
Yeah.

04:20.469 --> 04:22.805
Jade, Kenny, and a couple
of others, I think.

04:22.888 --> 04:25.391
Wow. I hope it works.

04:25.474 --> 04:28.352
We're gonna be up all night
making a rope ladder,

04:28.435 --> 04:29.645
if you wanna come by.

04:29.728 --> 04:31.772
Sounds like fun.

04:31.855 --> 04:34.024
Can you handle this?
I'm gonna go check the shed.

04:34.108 --> 04:35.359
-Yeah.
-Can I help?

04:35.442 --> 04:36.360
Sure.

04:37.569 --> 04:39.488
You're Clara.

04:39.571 --> 04:41.615
Yeah.
Um, Sophia, right?

04:41.699 --> 04:42.658
That's right.

04:42.741 --> 04:43.659
Hm.

04:43.742 --> 04:44.743
But, um...

04:46.912 --> 04:48.497
...do you know
who I really am?

04:48.580 --> 04:49.873
What?

04:49.957 --> 04:52.042
Maybe if you look closer.

04:53.919 --> 04:55.337
[chuckles uneasily]

05:03.595 --> 05:04.722
Does this help?

05:04.805 --> 05:06.557
Oh, God.

05:11.020 --> 05:12.646
Do you remember
the bargain we made?

05:15.107 --> 05:17.693
Good,

05:17.776 --> 05:19.778
because I need you
to do something for me.

05:21.572 --> 05:26.452
["Que Sera, Sera (Whatever Will
Be, Will Be)" plays]

05:31.498 --> 05:36.128
♪ When I was just a little boy ♪

05:36.211 --> 05:38.714
♪ I asked my father ♪

05:38.797 --> 05:40.424
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

05:42.551 --> 05:44.762
♪ "Will I be handsome?" ♪

05:44.845 --> 05:47.389
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

05:47.473 --> 05:51.393
♪ Here's what he said to me ♪

05:51.477 --> 05:54.354
♪ Que sera sera ♪

05:55.647 --> 05:58.776
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

06:00.527 --> 06:04.573
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

06:04.656 --> 06:07.451
♪ Que sera sera ♪

06:09.661 --> 06:12.581
♪ What will be will be ♪

06:21.965 --> 06:26.762
♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪

06:26.845 --> 06:29.098
♪ They ask their father ♪

06:29.181 --> 06:32.935
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

06:33.018 --> 06:35.521
♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪

06:35.604 --> 06:37.856
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

06:37.940 --> 06:40.400
♪ I tell them tenderly ♪

06:41.902 --> 06:44.571
♪ Que sera sera ♪

06:46.031 --> 06:49.159
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

06:50.869 --> 06:54.957
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

06:55.040 --> 06:57.417
♪ Que sera sera ♪

07:00.087 --> 07:03.006
♪ What will be will be ♪

07:05.300 --> 07:08.137
♪ Que sera sera ♪

07:25.571 --> 07:26.780
Hey.

07:26.864 --> 07:28.157
-Hey.
-What are you doing?

07:28.240 --> 07:29.491
How's Fatima?

07:29.575 --> 07:30.909
She's doing
the jigsaw puzzle.

07:30.993 --> 07:32.828
I told her
it was a cognitive test.

07:32.911 --> 07:35.831
Good; that should keep
her occupied for a bit.

07:35.914 --> 07:37.124
What are you looking for?

07:37.207 --> 07:38.876
Epinephrine shot
from the ambulance.

07:38.959 --> 07:40.544
I swear I put it in here.
I just...

07:42.838 --> 07:44.756
There it is.

07:44.840 --> 07:46.508
'Kay, I gotta go
to talk to Boyd.

07:46.592 --> 07:48.218
Just keep her here,
keep her busy.

07:48.302 --> 07:49.803
If anything happens,

07:49.887 --> 07:51.096
if her heart stops...

07:51.180 --> 07:52.723
Okay.
I've done these shots before.

07:52.806 --> 07:53.932
Right.

07:54.016 --> 07:58.061
-I got it.
-Just... be careful.

07:58.145 --> 07:59.855
We don't know what
any of this means yet.

07:59.938 --> 08:01.773
-Yeah.
-'Kay.

08:01.857 --> 08:02.816
I love you.

08:02.900 --> 08:04.026
Love you too.

08:04.109 --> 08:05.235
[sighs]

08:07.988 --> 08:09.198
Sara?

08:10.991 --> 08:12.492
Hello?

08:14.036 --> 08:15.078
You home?

08:23.921 --> 08:25.589
Come on in.

08:28.091 --> 08:29.092
[door slams]

08:31.386 --> 08:33.222
Let's go to my room.

08:41.730 --> 08:43.649
[tense music play]

08:49.363 --> 08:51.156
Sara painted it for me.

08:51.240 --> 08:53.200
Isn't that lovely?

08:54.785 --> 08:56.578
It's not my favorite color.

09:08.674 --> 09:10.175
Come sit.

09:12.761 --> 09:14.846
You don't have to be scared.

09:24.898 --> 09:29.027
When you first came here,
we made a bargain,

09:29.111 --> 09:30.362
and I told you,
at some point,

09:30.445 --> 09:33.073
that I was
gonna need your help.

09:33.156 --> 09:35.909
That day we met, I...

09:35.993 --> 09:38.287
started to wonder
if it was real.

09:38.370 --> 09:40.789
Are you really
gonna let me go home?

09:40.872 --> 09:43.000
First, you need to
help me with something.

09:44.751 --> 09:46.795
You want me to stop them
from digging up the bones.

09:46.878 --> 09:48.964
Oh, no.

09:49.047 --> 09:51.008
You see...

09:51.091 --> 09:55.721
when they go into
those tunnels tomorrow,

09:55.804 --> 09:59.099
that's not gonna
work out very well.

09:59.182 --> 10:01.184
They have
the right idea, of course,

10:01.268 --> 10:05.314
but this place...

10:05.397 --> 10:07.316
it's built on ritual,

10:08.942 --> 10:12.821
and with rituals,
how you do something

10:12.904 --> 10:16.158
is just as important
as what you do.

10:18.994 --> 10:20.954
Then, what do you
need from me?

10:23.498 --> 10:25.751
Do you like games, Clara?

10:27.252 --> 10:29.046
Answer me when
I ask you a question.

10:29.129 --> 10:32.799
Yes. Yeah,
I-I like games, I guess.

10:32.883 --> 10:35.052
I love them.

10:35.135 --> 10:38.680
I'm playing
so many right now, but...

10:38.764 --> 10:41.266
there's one or two

10:41.350 --> 10:44.227
that need a little push,

10:45.812 --> 10:46.813
speed things up a bit.

10:55.822 --> 10:57.741
Give me your hand.

10:59.951 --> 11:02.871
Clara, give me your hand

11:02.954 --> 11:05.749
or I'm going to do
horrible things to you.

11:12.255 --> 11:14.383
That's a good girl.

11:14.466 --> 11:15.926
[gasps]

11:22.099 --> 11:24.184
This next part
will feel strange.

11:27.270 --> 11:28.730
[gasps]

11:32.984 --> 11:34.444
Just relax.

11:38.115 --> 11:39.866
Let me in.

11:44.121 --> 11:45.288
[exhaling sharply]

11:45.372 --> 11:49.918
[breathing heavily]

11:56.341 --> 11:58.885
So, once the group in
the tunnels have the bones,

11:58.969 --> 12:02.389
then we pull the tree, and then
we get 'em out with the ladder

12:02.472 --> 12:04.766
that they're putting
together at the, uh, diner.

12:04.850 --> 12:06.226
And how are the people
in the tunnels

12:06.309 --> 12:08.437
gonna protect themselves
while they're digging?

12:08.520 --> 12:10.814
Those things down there
wake up, they're fucked!

12:10.897 --> 12:12.983
We're gonna cover the entrance
to the chamber with a tarp.

12:15.193 --> 12:16.778
We're gonna hang a talisman
on it, and it should be

12:16.862 --> 12:17.988
-as good as a wall.
-Yep.

12:18.071 --> 12:19.948
If the talismans
work down there.

12:20.031 --> 12:21.366
We haven't exactly
field-tested them yet.

12:21.450 --> 12:23.118
It'll work.

12:23.201 --> 12:25.036
Listen,
I don't wanna be the asshole,

12:25.120 --> 12:27.122
but once you pull out
that tree,

12:27.205 --> 12:29.249
it's like opening a window.

12:29.332 --> 12:32.210
Talismans or not, those
things are coming inside.

12:32.294 --> 12:33.837
[Donna sighs]

12:33.920 --> 12:35.797
Whoever's in that tunnel
is gonna get slaughtered

12:35.881 --> 12:38.467
long before they
climb that ladder.

12:38.550 --> 12:41.011
Once the bones
are out of the ground,

12:41.094 --> 12:42.387
they'll keep
the chamber safe.

12:42.471 --> 12:44.097
Come again?

12:44.181 --> 12:45.974
It's why they're buried.

12:46.057 --> 12:48.185
Those things down there
are afraid of them;

12:48.268 --> 12:50.228
I could feel it in my trip.

12:50.312 --> 12:51.897
Once we have the bones
out of the ground,

12:51.980 --> 12:54.483
they will keep those things
from coming into the chamber,

12:54.566 --> 12:56.151
at least long enough for
everyone to get out.

12:58.028 --> 12:59.863
You are putting a whole
lotta faith

12:59.946 --> 13:00.947
in a handful of mushrooms.

13:05.327 --> 13:09.122
Okay.
Let's say this works.

13:09.206 --> 13:11.249
Let's say you actually
dig up these magical bones

13:11.333 --> 13:13.543
and get outta
the chamber alive,

13:13.627 --> 13:15.212
what happens next?

13:16.922 --> 13:19.466
We all just gonna
hop in our cars and go home?

13:19.549 --> 13:21.384
We don't know.

13:21.468 --> 13:23.178
Of course not.

13:23.261 --> 13:24.721
You have figured out
just enough

13:24.804 --> 13:27.349
to get yourself killed, but not
what to do if you actually--

13:27.432 --> 13:29.935
Look, we can't wait around for
this prick in the yellow suit

13:30.018 --> 13:31.436
to keep picking us
off one by one!

13:31.520 --> 13:32.395
I know!

13:34.105 --> 13:36.525
I just hope you're right.

13:36.608 --> 13:37.526
[Kristi] Boyd?

13:39.110 --> 13:40.070
Kristi?

13:40.153 --> 13:42.614
-Can we talk?
-[Boyd] Wha...

13:42.697 --> 13:45.367
Um, Jade and I will go
get those radios started.

13:45.450 --> 13:47.911
Okay.
Uh, we'll finish.

13:49.454 --> 13:51.081
Hey, what's up?

13:51.164 --> 13:53.542
Let's-- yeah,
let's go for a walk.

13:53.625 --> 13:54.918
Come on.

13:57.629 --> 14:01.049
I, um, I don't
know how to say this,

14:01.132 --> 14:03.593
but Fatima is presenting
with the vital signs...

14:03.677 --> 14:05.845
[speaking inaudibly]

14:15.480 --> 14:17.065
You okay, Henry?

14:17.148 --> 14:19.526
Why is this here?

14:19.609 --> 14:21.570
-What?
-Did someone...

14:21.653 --> 14:23.905
bring it in their car?

14:23.989 --> 14:26.908
Who travels with
a carousel horse?

14:26.992 --> 14:29.452
I just figured
it was always here.

14:33.373 --> 14:34.624
I baked some cookies.
Do you want one?

14:37.544 --> 14:40.255
No, thank you.

14:40.338 --> 14:42.591
I don't blame you.

14:42.674 --> 14:46.428
I always used to bake
when I was nervous.

14:46.511 --> 14:48.972
It used to help with my...

14:55.186 --> 14:58.064
It used to help. But...

15:00.191 --> 15:03.111
...nothing ever really
turns out the same here.

15:03.194 --> 15:04.446
Yeah.

15:06.072 --> 15:07.949
Someone'll be hungry enough.

15:17.167 --> 15:18.627
[PA beeps, indistinct chatter]

15:18.710 --> 15:20.503
Dad? Dad.

15:20.587 --> 15:22.005
-It's okay.
-[Henry gasps]

15:22.088 --> 15:23.298
Hey.

15:23.381 --> 15:24.299
Hey!

15:24.382 --> 15:25.300
Hey. Okay. It's okay.

15:25.383 --> 15:26.384
Wha...

15:26.468 --> 15:27.510
Dad.

15:29.137 --> 15:31.640
Hey. Look,
I got your favorite.

15:34.392 --> 15:37.062
I even-- I brought some
provolone cheese from home.

15:38.229 --> 15:40.190
Here.

15:40.273 --> 15:43.985
Just like you like it.

15:44.069 --> 15:45.153
Yeah.

15:45.236 --> 15:46.237
Yeah?

15:51.826 --> 15:54.496
So, have you thought about

15:54.579 --> 15:56.665
what Doctor Boyd said?

15:56.748 --> 15:58.583
Doc-- Doctor Boyd?

15:58.667 --> 16:01.086
Yeah.

16:01.169 --> 16:02.629
That's-- That's right,

16:02.712 --> 16:04.464
the sheriff's name
is Boyd.

16:04.547 --> 16:06.091
How do you know that?

16:06.174 --> 16:08.176
Because you mumble
sometimes, Dad;

16:08.259 --> 16:10.178
so we've heard all the names -
Boyd and Donna,

16:10.261 --> 16:11.471
Ethan...

16:11.554 --> 16:12.555
I-I-I...

16:12.639 --> 16:14.015
Yeah.

16:14.099 --> 16:15.392
Okay. I'm, um, okay.

16:17.102 --> 16:19.020
Have you thought
about what she said

16:19.104 --> 16:20.689
about the anchor
that's keeping you there?

16:20.772 --> 16:23.274
[stammers]
Yeah, I can't-- I can't. No.

16:23.358 --> 16:24.567
Okay. Why?

16:24.651 --> 16:26.611
No, because...

16:26.695 --> 16:28.154
Because it's you.

16:29.781 --> 16:32.534
Victor, you're the anchor.
You're the anchor.

16:32.617 --> 16:34.744
You're-- You're--
you're what's keeping me there.

16:34.828 --> 16:37.163
So, the doctor wants me
to eliminate you?

16:37.247 --> 16:38.456
To kill you? No. I...

16:38.540 --> 16:40.040
Dad...

16:40.125 --> 16:42.335
-No!
-Dad, that's not me.

16:42.419 --> 16:45.588
No, that broken boy
who grew up alone,

16:45.672 --> 16:47.716
he's not-- he's not real.

16:47.799 --> 16:51.052
He's not real, Dad.
Look at me.

16:51.136 --> 16:55.056
I'm not alone.
I'm here.

16:55.140 --> 16:56.224
Yeah.

16:56.307 --> 16:57.308
Okay.

16:57.392 --> 16:58.476
I have a family,

16:58.560 --> 17:00.729
one that misses
you very much.

17:00.812 --> 17:02.564
And if what the doctor
is saying is true,

17:02.647 --> 17:04.733
and you just let go of that--
that version of me,

17:04.816 --> 17:06.276
then you get
to come back to us.

17:06.358 --> 17:07.527
Isn't that what you want?

17:07.609 --> 17:08.611
Don't you want that?

17:08.694 --> 17:10.780
Well, of course. Of c...

17:12.781 --> 17:14.742
But how--
how could I? Even if--

17:14.826 --> 17:19.079
Even if I wanted to,
how could I...?

17:19.164 --> 17:21.249
You know,
with my bare hands? Or...

17:21.332 --> 17:22.834
Dad, the doctor
said that

17:22.916 --> 17:25.211
once you accept
that it's a dream,

17:25.295 --> 17:27.630
the dream is gonna provide you
with everything that you need.

17:27.714 --> 17:29.466
You just need
to accept it isn't real.

17:29.549 --> 17:30.759
But how can I do that?!

17:30.842 --> 17:32.427
[gasp]

17:32.510 --> 17:34.220
[Victor] Dad?

17:34.304 --> 17:35.722
-[groans]
-Dad?

17:37.599 --> 17:38.767
Are you okay?

17:41.478 --> 17:43.521
[clears throat]

17:43.605 --> 17:45.482
I'm-- I'm fine.

17:45.565 --> 17:47.150
Well, you don't look fine.

17:49.360 --> 17:50.612
I'm...

17:50.695 --> 17:52.322
-Dad, please--
-I...

17:52.405 --> 17:54.783
need you to just...

17:54.866 --> 17:56.242
I need to be alone
right now.

17:59.454 --> 18:00.747
Dad...

18:00.830 --> 18:02.457
[door closes]

18:02.540 --> 18:04.459
And where is she now?

18:04.542 --> 18:06.544
We're trying to keep her at
the clinic as long as possible.

18:06.628 --> 18:08.421
Marielle's up there
with her now.

18:08.505 --> 18:09.589
Okay.

18:13.843 --> 18:15.303
Boyd, what's the plan here?

18:15.386 --> 18:16.721
I don't know.

18:16.805 --> 18:18.223
Okay, you're gonna have to
do a bit better than that.

18:18.306 --> 18:19.849
I can't, all right? I'm--

18:21.476 --> 18:22.811
Okay.

18:22.894 --> 18:24.687
Okay, how 'bout
we talk to Ellis?

18:24.771 --> 18:26.314
No. No.

18:26.397 --> 18:30.193
You do not talk to Ellis.
You don't talk to Fatima.

18:30.276 --> 18:32.320
The best thing
we can do right now

18:32.403 --> 18:33.488
is get her
the fuck outta here,

18:33.571 --> 18:35.448
and that means
tomorrow has to work.

18:35.532 --> 18:36.741
Okay, I'm gonna need you
to come out there.

18:36.825 --> 18:38.535
-Boyd, I--
-We got a group of people

18:38.618 --> 18:40.286
going down into those tunnels.

18:40.370 --> 18:41.579
I don't know
what kinda shape

18:41.663 --> 18:42.789
they're gonna be in
when they come out.

18:42.872 --> 18:44.582
Somebody gets hurt,
we might not have time

18:44.666 --> 18:45.834
to make it to the clinic.

18:45.917 --> 18:49.254
So, Marielle
stays with Fatima,

18:49.337 --> 18:52.340
you bring as many supplies as
you can out to the Bottle Tree.

18:52.423 --> 18:54.843
We're gonna--
we're gonna get through this.

18:56.761 --> 18:59.931
And then, we're--
we're gonna go home.

19:00.014 --> 19:01.474
We are gonna go home.

19:04.936 --> 19:06.396
What? What do you mean
he was here?

19:06.479 --> 19:07.438
He was in the house?

19:10.275 --> 19:11.568
Yeah.

19:12.485 --> 19:15.238
Why didn't the talisman
stop him from coming in?

19:16.781 --> 19:17.907
I don't know.

19:19.784 --> 19:21.244
Is he the one
that killed Dad?

19:25.665 --> 19:26.749
Yes.

19:28.501 --> 19:30.420
Was it because what you
and Jade figured out?

19:30.503 --> 19:32.797
Is that what "knowledge
comes at a cost" means?

19:35.008 --> 19:35.925
Yes.

19:37.677 --> 19:40.263
[Julie]
Okay, so, who's next?

19:40.346 --> 19:42.348
You're still looking
for answers, right?

19:43.725 --> 19:45.602
Who's he gonna kill next?

19:45.685 --> 19:47.353
Ethan?

19:47.437 --> 19:49.272
Me?

19:49.355 --> 19:50.690
I'm not going
to let that happen.

19:50.773 --> 19:53.651
How? How are you
gonna stop that, Mom?

19:53.735 --> 19:55.778
Can't you see what
this place is doing to you?

19:55.862 --> 19:58.573
It lies.
Do you honestly believe

19:58.656 --> 20:00.783
that you've been here over
and over and over again?

20:00.867 --> 20:02.952
That you're
some kind of ancient savior?

20:04.746 --> 20:06.581
I saw
the Man in Yellow once.

20:08.958 --> 20:10.793
I saw him standing
in the middle of the street,

20:10.877 --> 20:11.920
eating a bunch
of dead people.

20:12.003 --> 20:13.421
Wait. What?

20:13.504 --> 20:15.840
I thought that I was
traveling through time,

20:15.924 --> 20:18.927
that I could change things
and that I could save Dad.

20:19.010 --> 20:21.012
But you know what
I was really doing?

20:21.095 --> 20:22.889
I was giving
myself seizures.

20:26.976 --> 20:28.561
Where are you going?

20:32.857 --> 20:34.484
Are you okay?

20:36.527 --> 20:37.654
I'm fine.

20:39.072 --> 20:41.407
How do these work?

20:41.491 --> 20:43.576
Who made them?
Did you make them?

20:45.787 --> 20:47.538
I don't know.

20:47.622 --> 20:48.623
But if you have
all these memories,

20:48.706 --> 20:50.375
you should know this, right?

20:50.458 --> 20:51.960
It doesn't work that way.

20:52.043 --> 20:53.753
Maybe that's
because it's not real.

20:55.046 --> 20:56.714
Mom...

20:56.798 --> 20:59.300
this place lies
to us so that

20:59.384 --> 21:00.843
we hurt ourselves
and we hurt each other.

21:02.553 --> 21:04.514
Please stop
giving it what it wants.

21:14.440 --> 21:19.320
[pensive music playing]

21:27.578 --> 21:31.374
[ominous music playing]

21:31.457 --> 21:32.625
[winces]

21:35.795 --> 21:37.505
[groans]

21:39.757 --> 21:40.717
[winces]

21:55.648 --> 21:59.569
[ominous music playing]

22:07.076 --> 22:08.828
-[Marielle] Hey.
-Hey.

22:08.911 --> 22:10.038
Everything okay?

22:10.121 --> 22:12.832
Yeah. I, um...

22:12.915 --> 22:15.501
I just brought
something for Fatima.

22:15.585 --> 22:17.086
A family remedy.

22:17.170 --> 22:18.546
Uh, she's inside.

22:18.629 --> 22:20.048
Great.

22:27.930 --> 22:29.390
Hey, Fatima.

22:29.474 --> 22:30.600
Hey.

22:30.683 --> 22:32.143
What are you doing here?

22:32.226 --> 22:35.063
I heard you weren't feeling
great, so I made this for you.

22:35.146 --> 22:37.523
What is it?

22:37.607 --> 22:39.692
It's, uh,
an old family recipe,

22:39.776 --> 22:42.070
a mix of berries, herbs.

22:42.153 --> 22:44.655
I had to improvise with
a couple of ingredients.

22:44.739 --> 22:47.450
That's very sweet.
Thank you.

22:51.829 --> 22:53.498
You really need to drink it
while it's fresh.

22:55.166 --> 22:57.460
It'll make you feel better;
I promise.

22:58.961 --> 23:02.465
Uh, yeah. Sure.

23:02.548 --> 23:04.634
Can't hurt, right?

23:15.269 --> 23:17.021
[chuckling nervously]

23:17.105 --> 23:18.773
I know it doesn't
taste great, but, um...

23:20.149 --> 23:22.110
Take care of yourself.

23:22.193 --> 23:23.861
I'll see you back
at Colony House.

23:23.945 --> 23:25.071
Yeah.

23:49.554 --> 23:51.722
I'm sorry
I don't come here much.

23:54.767 --> 23:57.019
But I don't really know
what to think anymore.

23:59.021 --> 24:02.900
Boyd told Dad and I
that you're Tabitha now.

24:05.069 --> 24:06.612
If you're Tabitha,

24:06.696 --> 24:09.532
that means that
you're not with Eloise.

24:14.745 --> 24:16.706
That means
you're not even there.

24:21.669 --> 24:23.462
But I don't know
where else to go.

24:26.591 --> 24:28.718
I think there's
something wrong with Dad,

24:28.801 --> 24:30.469
and I-I don't know
how to help him.

24:34.015 --> 24:37.018
Tabitha says that
we're gonna go home...

24:41.647 --> 24:44.859
...but what if he doesn't
make it that long?

24:44.942 --> 24:49.530
I don't know things that I'm
supposed to say to someone.

24:57.622 --> 24:59.207
Go away.

24:59.290 --> 25:00.750
This is private.

25:03.669 --> 25:05.004
What do you want?

25:05.087 --> 25:07.256
You know what
the others are doing?

25:08.966 --> 25:10.635
Going into the tunnels
to get the bones,

25:10.718 --> 25:12.553
so everyone can go home.

25:12.637 --> 25:15.139
Did you know they're
gonna pull down the tree?

25:17.099 --> 25:18.726
The Bottle Tree?

25:18.809 --> 25:20.686
I've told
you before;

25:20.770 --> 25:22.939
that tree is important.

25:23.022 --> 25:25.233
You can't let that happen!

25:30.321 --> 25:33.199
I just want
you to know...

25:34.784 --> 25:36.244
that I'm
not here for me.

25:38.371 --> 25:40.623
I don't
fuckin' like you.

25:42.083 --> 25:44.335
I think I've made
that pretty clear.

25:44.418 --> 25:46.712
I've made peace with...

25:46.796 --> 25:49.924
whatever shit
you got planned for me.

25:50.007 --> 25:52.635
I'm here for my son.

25:54.136 --> 25:55.846
I'm here for Fatima.

25:59.850 --> 26:03.145
Don't do this.
You hear me?

26:03.229 --> 26:07.733
Whatever this shit is
you're pulling, don't do this.

26:07.817 --> 26:09.986
Whatever it is
you have against me,

26:10.069 --> 26:13.281
there are good
people here.

26:13.364 --> 26:16.784
Get these people home!
You--

26:16.867 --> 26:18.077
Boyd?

26:19.704 --> 26:22.331
Kristi said you were
looking for me.

26:28.879 --> 26:31.299
I need to ask you not to repeat
anything I'm about to say.

26:31.382 --> 26:32.842
Okay?

26:32.925 --> 26:33.968
Of course.

26:35.469 --> 26:37.013
All right.

26:38.931 --> 26:42.101
Fatima is down at the clinic,
having some tests done.

26:43.477 --> 26:45.730
Uh, her heart rate,

26:45.813 --> 26:47.315
her blood pressure are not...

26:49.859 --> 26:51.819
She should be dead
right now.

26:53.404 --> 26:56.032
But, instead, she's walking
around like nothing's wrong.

26:59.076 --> 27:01.704
When Fatima went missing,

27:01.787 --> 27:06.667
you came to me and you said
the voices were laughing.

27:06.751 --> 27:10.338
Right? Because they knew
that I couldn't save her.

27:11.922 --> 27:13.132
But we did.
We found her.

27:14.759 --> 27:16.135
She's okay.

27:17.511 --> 27:19.055
The voices were wrong.

27:21.432 --> 27:24.060
We-- We saved her.

27:24.143 --> 27:25.853
Didn't we?

27:27.772 --> 27:29.774
I don't know.

27:32.943 --> 27:33.903
Okay.

27:33.986 --> 27:36.197
I'm coming
with you tomorrow.

27:38.074 --> 27:40.368
I wanna be there.

27:43.913 --> 27:47.833
[indistinct chatter in distance]

27:56.342 --> 27:57.927
[door opens]

28:00.554 --> 28:01.764
Hey.

28:07.478 --> 28:09.897
Do you think
he was really Dad?

28:11.482 --> 28:12.942
What?

28:13.025 --> 28:15.027
We went to the settlement

28:15.111 --> 28:17.947
because Dad told me
to find the Lake of Tears.

28:18.030 --> 28:20.032
Then, bad things happened.

28:22.118 --> 28:23.786
Do you think
it was really him?

28:25.579 --> 28:27.456
I don't know, honey.

28:27.540 --> 28:29.208
[exhales heavily]

28:31.210 --> 28:34.922
I think this place
tries to make us afraid,

28:35.005 --> 28:37.425
so we won't believe in
the things that can help us.

28:37.508 --> 28:39.468
All those things
you remember?

28:41.220 --> 28:43.931
You should listen to
what it's trying to tell you.

28:44.014 --> 28:45.391
Don't be scared
to believe.

28:48.018 --> 28:50.438
Come here. Come here.

28:58.195 --> 29:01.407
[ominous music playing]

29:20.384 --> 29:21.302
Mom?

29:25.431 --> 29:26.765
What's wrong?

29:34.231 --> 29:37.902
And we boosted the signal
as much as we could.

29:37.985 --> 29:41.989
We're not gonna be able to talk
to each other, but we do have...

29:42.072 --> 29:43.991
[static beeping]

29:44.074 --> 29:45.534
Huh?

29:45.618 --> 29:48.287
Poor man's Morse code.

29:48.370 --> 29:50.247
So, you can signal us
from the chamber.

29:50.331 --> 29:51.582
Exactly.

29:51.665 --> 29:53.083
Okay, that's good.

29:53.167 --> 29:54.835
-Nice.
-Pack all this up

29:54.919 --> 29:56.003
and bring it
to Colony House.

29:56.086 --> 29:58.464
-Yes, sir.
-Yeah, we need to-- Victor?

29:58.547 --> 30:02.301
Is it true?
Are you pulling down the tree?

30:02.384 --> 30:04.094
The Bottle Tree,
are you pulling it down?

30:04.178 --> 30:06.055
We need to make sure that
we can get our people

30:06.138 --> 30:07.264
out of the tunnels safely.

30:07.348 --> 30:09.016
-You can't do that!
-We don't have a choice.

30:09.099 --> 30:10.309
Victor, this is a good thing.

30:10.392 --> 30:12.269
No, you don't understand.
He said you can't.

30:12.353 --> 30:14.396
-Wait. Who said?
-The Boy in White;

30:14.480 --> 30:16.482
he said that
the tree is important.

30:18.400 --> 30:19.485
You can't pull it down.

30:19.568 --> 30:21.403
Because the Boy in White
said not to.

30:21.487 --> 30:22.613
-That's right.
-Okay, then,

30:22.696 --> 30:24.532
where is he, Victor?
Why doesn't he just come

30:24.615 --> 30:26.492
-in here and tell us himself?
-It doesn't work that way!

30:26.575 --> 30:28.619
He told me! He's my friend,
and he knows things!

30:28.702 --> 30:30.871
Why won't he help us?

30:30.955 --> 30:32.164
Victor, there are things here,

30:32.248 --> 30:33.874
there are things here
that play games with us.

30:33.958 --> 30:35.376
-No.
-And I think this little boy

30:35.459 --> 30:36.502
is one of those things.

30:36.585 --> 30:39.046
No! No!
You-- you can't do this!

30:39.129 --> 30:42.299
You can't!
I'm gonna stop you!

30:42.383 --> 30:44.218
Hey, Vic-- Aww, fuck.

30:44.301 --> 30:45.636
Victor, listen, hey.

30:45.719 --> 30:47.388
Victor?
Listen to me.

30:47.471 --> 30:49.890
Slow down.
Victor, slow down.

30:49.974 --> 30:51.058
No.

30:51.141 --> 30:52.560
Victor, hey, Buddy.
Hey, listen.

30:52.643 --> 30:54.895
I'm gonna need you to come
with me to the station, Victor!

30:54.979 --> 30:56.272
Okay?
Victor, come here.

30:56.355 --> 30:58.107
-Get off me!
-Hey, Victor, come on!

30:58.190 --> 30:59.984
-No! No!
-Come!

31:00.067 --> 31:02.403
-No, no! No!
-Take it easy!

31:02.486 --> 31:04.613
-No, no!
-[Boyd] Okay, Victor, all right.

31:04.697 --> 31:07.533
Stop!
[screaming]

31:07.616 --> 31:09.410
Stop it!
I am trying to help you!

31:09.493 --> 31:10.953
-I know!
-I'm trying to help you!

31:11.036 --> 31:12.329
Yes, Victor.
I know, I know, I know.

31:12.413 --> 31:13.914
-I'm sorry, buddy.
-[screaming]

31:13.998 --> 31:16.292
I know, I know, I know.
There are people...

31:16.375 --> 31:18.627
-You don't understand!
-...risking their lives,

31:18.711 --> 31:19.962
and we just can't take...

31:20.045 --> 31:21.922
-Stop!
-...any chances.

31:22.006 --> 31:24.341
Okay! Okay.
Come on, come on, come on.

31:24.425 --> 31:26.176
-Tabitha! Stop!
-No! Wait, wait, wait!

31:26.260 --> 31:27.553
Don't let them do it!
Don't let them!

31:27.636 --> 31:29.138
Take him to the station,
all right?

31:29.221 --> 31:31.265
-'Kay, Victor, come on!
-Why is he in handcuffs?!

31:31.348 --> 31:34.560
Because I'm trying to prevent
a problem before it happens.

31:34.643 --> 31:37.187
The Boy in White told him that
we can't take down the tree,

31:37.271 --> 31:39.648
so he's gonna try and stop us.

31:39.732 --> 31:42.109
Look, you tell me you wanna
scrap this whole thing,

31:42.192 --> 31:44.653
forget about the bones,
then I'll let Victor go.

31:44.737 --> 31:46.322
We don't know who
the boy is or what he wants.

31:46.405 --> 31:49.158
Exactly! Exactly.
Excuse me.

31:49.241 --> 31:51.285
Boyd, wait.

31:51.368 --> 31:52.703
It needs to be me.

31:52.786 --> 31:55.122
I need to be the one who
goes down into the tunnels,

31:55.205 --> 31:57.333
Hey, we've got plenty of people
going down there, and--

31:57.416 --> 31:59.460
Boyd, you don't understand.

31:59.543 --> 32:01.337
It needs to be
only me and Jade.

32:01.420 --> 32:04.298
What?
Hold on, this--

32:04.381 --> 32:05.591
Boyd, we're the ones

32:05.674 --> 32:08.093
who failed to save
those children.

32:08.177 --> 32:10.638
We're the ones they've been
calling to over and over again.

32:12.264 --> 32:14.058
Okay, listen, look.

32:14.141 --> 32:16.352
Look, look, look, look, look.
Look at the talisman.

32:16.435 --> 32:19.146
There are
two people here, right?

32:19.229 --> 32:21.148
Who do you
think those people are?

32:21.231 --> 32:22.441
It has to be us.

32:24.401 --> 32:26.403
I ca-- I can't. I can't.

32:26.487 --> 32:29.657
Something goes wrong, what
happens to Julie and Ethan?

32:29.740 --> 32:31.367
Who do you think
I'm doing this for?

32:31.450 --> 32:33.285
Boyd...

32:33.369 --> 32:35.162
we only get
to do this once.

32:36.580 --> 32:39.041
And I think here,
in this place,

32:40.417 --> 32:42.961
the way that
we do this matters.

32:44.755 --> 32:47.049
You have to trust me.

32:50.844 --> 32:54.973
[bell ringing]

33:04.566 --> 33:06.485
[bell ringing]

33:09.488 --> 33:10.531
Time to get inside.

33:10.614 --> 33:12.032
Oh, um,
I thought I'd help out

33:12.116 --> 33:13.409
with the rope ladder
in the diner.

33:13.492 --> 33:15.536
It seems really important.

33:15.619 --> 33:18.330
They'll really
appreciate that; we all do.

33:18.414 --> 33:20.457
Just doing my part.
Goodnight, Sheriff.

33:20.541 --> 33:21.792
Night.

33:21.875 --> 33:26.004
[bell ringing]

33:29.758 --> 33:32.261
[indistinct quiet chatter]

33:32.344 --> 33:34.054
Those buttons don't
actually work.

33:34.138 --> 33:35.556
You know,
they're just for show.

33:38.684 --> 33:40.394
["Doctor My Eyes" plays]

33:40.477 --> 33:42.229
How did you do that?

33:42.312 --> 33:43.480
What do you mean?

33:49.862 --> 33:51.405
[screeching]

33:51.488 --> 33:54.575
♪ Doctor, my eyes
have seen the years ♪

33:54.658 --> 33:56.744
♪ And the slow
parade of fears ♪

33:56.827 --> 33:59.288
♪ Without crying ♪

33:59.371 --> 34:02.332
♪ Now I want to understand ♪

34:04.209 --> 34:06.837
♪ I have done
all that I could ♪

34:06.920 --> 34:08.547
♪ To see the evil
and the good ♪

34:08.630 --> 34:10.257
[gasps]

34:10.340 --> 34:11.632
♪ Without hiding ♪

34:11.717 --> 34:13.635
What are you guys
doing in there?

34:13.719 --> 34:15.846
Jesus, those fucking things...

34:15.929 --> 34:18.556
-♪ Doctor, my eyes ♪
-Just ignore them.

34:20.684 --> 34:22.811
♪ Tell me what is wrong ♪

34:22.895 --> 34:25.647
♪ Was I unwise... ♪

34:25.731 --> 34:28.692
Stay focused, you guys.
All right? Just keep working.

34:31.360 --> 34:33.447
Let's get those blinds closed.

34:33.530 --> 34:35.157
[groaning in pain]

34:35.239 --> 34:37.701
♪ 'Cause I have wandered
through this world ♪

34:37.784 --> 34:39.328
[groans]

34:39.411 --> 34:42.206
♪ And as each moment
has unfurled ♪

34:42.289 --> 34:43.665
♪ I've been waiting ♪

34:43.748 --> 34:46.710
♪ To awaken
from these dreams ♪

34:48.545 --> 34:51.715
♪ People go just
where they will ♪

34:51.799 --> 34:53.884
♪ I never
noticed them until ♪

34:53.967 --> 34:56.469
♪ I got this feeling ♪

34:56.553 --> 35:00.265
♪ That it's later
than it seems ♪

35:00.349 --> 35:02.309
♪ Doctor, my eyes ♪

35:02.392 --> 35:04.895
[groaning in pain]

35:04.978 --> 35:06.355
♪ Tell me what you see ♪

35:06.438 --> 35:10.234
♪ I hear their cries ♪

35:10.317 --> 35:13.153
♪ Just say if it's
too late for me ♪

35:13.237 --> 35:14.196
[groaning in pain]

35:14.279 --> 35:17.616
[moaning]

35:20.911 --> 35:23.497
[Kenny]
He's just sitting there.

35:23.580 --> 35:27.251
Yeah, he's angry
and he's scared.

35:30.254 --> 35:31.672
Hey, look.

35:32.464 --> 35:34.383
There's something
we need to talk about.

35:36.301 --> 35:38.595
You're not coming
out there with us tomorrow.

35:38.679 --> 35:40.305
-What?
-I need you to stay behind.

35:40.389 --> 35:41.348
No.

35:41.431 --> 35:43.350
Kenny, listen to me.

35:43.433 --> 35:45.727
Listen to me.
All planning aside,

35:45.811 --> 35:48.522
we have no idea what's
gonna happen tomorrow.

35:48.605 --> 35:50.691
If we end up looking
at the worst-case scenario,

35:50.774 --> 35:52.401
okay?

35:53.443 --> 35:56.321
Donna's gonna need some help
keeping this place together.

35:56.405 --> 35:58.574
Think of it like a...

35:58.657 --> 36:02.202
a continuity of government
in the event of a catastrophe.

36:02.286 --> 36:03.704
You want me to just sit here--

36:03.787 --> 36:05.831
I want you to do your part.

36:08.542 --> 36:10.586
You asked me to stand down

36:10.669 --> 36:14.381
when I wanted to be the one
to test the totem, and, hey,

36:14.464 --> 36:16.216
you were right.

36:16.300 --> 36:18.385
I'm asking you
to stand down now.

36:20.721 --> 36:22.306
Please.

36:26.310 --> 36:27.394
Okay.

36:34.443 --> 36:37.613
The last of
Father Khatri's stash.

36:47.998 --> 36:49.291
[clears throat]

36:55.839 --> 36:57.507
To better days.

36:57.591 --> 36:58.717
Yeah.

36:58.800 --> 37:00.844
To better days.

37:00.928 --> 37:02.262
[glasses clink]

37:11.021 --> 37:12.230
I know.

37:13.732 --> 37:15.525
[Ethan] Why can't we just
stay at the house?

37:15.609 --> 37:17.986
Honey,
you'll be safer here.

37:18.070 --> 37:19.988
Can't somebody else
go down in the tunnels?

37:20.072 --> 37:22.532
I wish they could,
but it has to be me.

37:24.868 --> 37:26.995
Don't be scared
to believe, remember?

37:27.079 --> 37:28.747
What if you
don't come back?

37:28.830 --> 37:31.458
Hey.
Remember what Jade said.

37:31.541 --> 37:34.044
The bones are gonna protect us
when we're down in the chamber.

37:34.127 --> 37:35.837
And once we're back,

37:35.921 --> 37:38.340
we'll be
so much closer to going home.

37:41.843 --> 37:43.261
How are the bones
gonna protect you?

37:46.056 --> 37:48.684
It's just the way they work.

37:48.767 --> 37:50.811
See?

37:50.894 --> 37:52.396
We're going to be okay.

37:58.068 --> 37:59.611
I love you.

38:02.030 --> 38:03.657
You gotta
be strong, okay?

38:03.740 --> 38:05.701
[Ethan] Okay.

38:05.784 --> 38:07.911
-[Tabitha] Okay.
-We should get going.

38:12.082 --> 38:13.917
I'll see you
in a few hours.

38:15.794 --> 38:16.878
I love you.

38:16.962 --> 38:18.547
I love you too.

38:29.057 --> 38:30.517
You're lucky.

38:30.600 --> 38:33.103
Why's that?

38:33.186 --> 38:35.480
Not a single person here
tried to talk me out of this.

38:38.692 --> 38:40.527
Hey, Acosta,
you get that ladder off.

38:40.610 --> 38:43.530
-Got it?
-Yeah.

38:43.613 --> 38:45.532
-Goin' up, Randall?
-[Randall] Yeah.

38:45.615 --> 38:47.034
Whoa. Wait, wait, wait, wait.
Make sure.

38:47.117 --> 38:48.994
Yeah, yeah. Okay.

38:49.077 --> 38:50.537
Hey, anything yet?

38:50.620 --> 38:52.372
-Think we've got something.
-[static hisses]

38:52.456 --> 38:54.541
Rope ladder's here.

38:54.624 --> 38:55.876
[Kristi] Oh, okay, great.
Come over here.

38:55.959 --> 38:56.793
[Acosta] Here, I'll help you.

38:58.962 --> 39:00.881
[static beeps]

39:00.964 --> 39:01.965
Radios are online.

39:02.049 --> 39:03.925
You ready?

39:04.009 --> 39:05.761
Not really.

39:05.844 --> 39:07.721
That's the right answer.

39:07.804 --> 39:09.431
Oh, come on. Okay.

39:18.565 --> 39:19.816
Watch your head.

39:19.900 --> 39:20.942
[Tabitha] Yeah!

39:51.890 --> 39:54.935
[ominous music playing]

39:58.563 --> 39:59.731
[door opens]

40:02.734 --> 40:04.528
What are you doing here?

40:04.611 --> 40:07.114
I thought you'd want to know;
things changed a little,

40:07.197 --> 40:09.449
and now it's only
Tabitha and Jade

40:09.533 --> 40:11.159
who are going
into the tunnels.

40:15.580 --> 40:17.207
You should've told me sooner.

40:17.290 --> 40:20.460
I'm sorry.
I just found out.

40:20.544 --> 40:22.170
I-I still get
to go home, right?

40:24.089 --> 40:26.133
Sophia?

40:26.216 --> 40:28.135
Check this out. There's a--
There's a--

40:28.218 --> 40:32.222
there's a
person in this photo, um...

40:32.305 --> 40:34.766
the girl in the background...

40:34.850 --> 40:36.935
she looks just like you.

40:41.189 --> 40:42.732
That's because it is me.

40:44.734 --> 40:46.736
I don't understand.
How is that possible?

40:49.239 --> 40:52.868
Clara, would you
lock the doors, please?

40:56.621 --> 40:59.499
[door opens]

40:59.583 --> 41:02.043
I can only take the form of
people who have died here.

41:04.754 --> 41:06.882
The hell's going on?

41:06.965 --> 41:09.092
I really wish you
hadn't seen that.

41:09.176 --> 41:10.218
[lock clicks]

41:19.603 --> 41:20.896
This is it.

41:26.193 --> 41:28.028
Here. Here.

41:29.988 --> 41:31.531
Take this.

41:38.205 --> 41:39.998
[breathing unsteadily]

41:40.081 --> 41:41.041
[tape screeches]

41:41.124 --> 41:42.542
Hurry.

41:42.626 --> 41:44.711
Okay, listen.
Just breathe, okay?

41:44.794 --> 41:46.213
Once we're done,
we're safe.

41:46.296 --> 41:47.881
Okay.

41:49.257 --> 41:50.717
-[tape screeches]
-Sorry.

41:50.800 --> 41:52.093
Tabitha, take this.
Here. Got it?

41:52.177 --> 41:53.094
Okay.

41:53.178 --> 41:54.763
Right over here.

41:54.846 --> 41:55.764
Yep.

41:57.641 --> 41:58.725
[tape screeches]

41:58.808 --> 42:00.060
Hurry up.

42:01.978 --> 42:03.897
Okay. Okay.

42:03.980 --> 42:06.274
Okay. It's good.

42:06.358 --> 42:08.276
It's good.

42:08.360 --> 42:09.778
[Boyd] Hey, wait, wait.
Watch your fingers,

42:09.861 --> 42:11.571
watch your fingers,
watch the fingers.

42:11.655 --> 42:13.031
-It's ready.
-Make sure it's secure.

42:13.114 --> 42:14.282
-You got it?
-Great. Yep.

42:14.366 --> 42:17.077
Yeah. They're in the chamber.

42:17.160 --> 42:18.745
Okay.

42:18.828 --> 42:20.956
All right, guys, let's get
that truck into position.

42:21.039 --> 42:22.707
On the next signal, we go.

42:22.791 --> 42:23.959
Yeah.

42:24.042 --> 42:25.794
[Kristi]
'Kay, everyone get back!

42:25.877 --> 42:27.754
[Ellis]
All right. Let's go!

42:31.841 --> 42:33.885
Here you go.

42:39.849 --> 42:41.309
This is it.

42:43.186 --> 42:44.771
This is where
they're buried.

42:51.945 --> 42:52.862
Okay...

43:02.330 --> 43:07.168
[shovels digging in distance]

43:10.130 --> 43:12.173
[shovels echoing]

43:16.303 --> 43:18.179
[ominous music playing]

43:27.814 --> 43:29.733
[shovels continue digging]

43:40.243 --> 43:41.786
[shovels continue digging]

43:41.870 --> 43:42.871
[straining]

43:48.376 --> 43:52.380
[suspenseful music playing]

43:54.883 --> 43:57.052
[clanks]

43:59.471 --> 44:00.388
[clanks]

44:01.765 --> 44:03.099
Tabitha.

44:03.183 --> 44:04.267
You found it.

44:04.351 --> 44:05.935
Oh, God.

44:06.019 --> 44:06.936
Yes.

44:08.021 --> 44:08.980
Yes.

44:11.358 --> 44:12.901
[Jade]
Look.

44:14.944 --> 44:16.196
Help me find the edges.

44:16.279 --> 44:17.197
Yeah.

44:19.032 --> 44:21.826
[clanking]

44:21.910 --> 44:23.912
[ominous music playing]

44:30.960 --> 44:31.920
Okay.

44:33.338 --> 44:35.799
Okay. That's good.
Let's grab the crowbars.

44:35.882 --> 44:37.092
-Okay.
-That's fine.

44:37.175 --> 44:40.845
[suspenseful music playing]

44:40.929 --> 44:43.014
[ominous music playing]

44:47.143 --> 44:48.395
-Stick it under the rock.
-What?

44:48.478 --> 44:49.813
Stick it under the rock.

44:49.896 --> 44:51.940
That's it.
Get some leverage on it.

44:52.023 --> 44:53.358
-Yeah.
-Let's lift. Okay, ready?

44:53.441 --> 44:54.901
-Yeah.
-One, two, three!

44:54.984 --> 44:57.278
[groans with effort]

44:57.362 --> 44:59.030
[gasping]

44:59.114 --> 45:01.282
-Oh, damn, that's heavy!
-Why is this so difficult?

45:01.366 --> 45:03.076
It's a giant slab of rock.

45:03.159 --> 45:04.244
Okay, ready?

45:04.327 --> 45:05.870
One, two, three!

45:05.954 --> 45:07.038
[grunts]

45:07.122 --> 45:11.418
[grunting in distance]

45:11.501 --> 45:13.294
Okay.

45:13.378 --> 45:15.797
Wait, wait, wait.

45:15.880 --> 45:18.925
Ready? Okay.

45:19.008 --> 45:20.927
[both straining]

45:21.010 --> 45:24.055
[straining]

45:24.139 --> 45:25.932
[Tabitha]
Okay.

45:26.015 --> 45:27.892
Okay. Okay.

45:30.395 --> 45:32.063
Oh, Jesus.

45:33.606 --> 45:35.191
[breathing heavily]

45:46.369 --> 45:48.496
[creature] You know, you really
shouldn't be doing that.

45:50.165 --> 45:51.833
Jade...

45:53.460 --> 45:55.336
[theme music plays]
